Description: The Desktop page's error state without Ubuntu's name
 Ubuntu's page, which Patrone calls Desktop, said "No Ubuntu settings
 found" and asked for a bug report in Launchpad, Ubuntu's bug tracker, when
 it couldn't read the desktop's settings. Patrone's words don't point at
 Ubuntu (docs/COMPLIANCE.md, item 18).
Author: William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/panels/ubuntu/cc-ubuntu-panel.blp
+++ b/panels/ubuntu/cc-ubuntu-panel.blp
@@ -33,13 +33,13 @@
         Label {
           margin-top: 12;
           wrap: true;
-          label: _("No Ubuntu settings found");
+          label: _("No desktop settings found");
         }

         [end]
         Label {
           wrap: true;
-          label: _("Oops, something has gone wrong. Please report a bug in Launchpad.");
+          label: _("Something has gone wrong: the desktop's settings couldn't be read.");

           attributes: "scale 1.42";
         }
